# Whether every side the mode commands, and every physical side, has its linear
# track at a target (ADR-0067, ADR-0070; safety findings SA2c-S-02 c, S-08).
#
# A program driving the pair through the twin boundary reads its OWN domain's
# joint states, which are the plant's; the counterpart's are on a domain the
# program never opens (ADR-0044 clause 3). So before it starts the next step it
# asks the boundary, which already reads every side's joint states, whether each
# side the current mode commands (`cite_twin.routing.commanded_sides`), and every
# physical side whatever the mode, stands within `tolerance_m` of `position_m`.
# The boundary answers a verdict and not the positions: the reverse state flow
# is consumed by L5 and republished nowhere (ADR-0050 decision 1b).
#
# A physical side's position counts only while it is fresh (the plan's
# `state_max_age_s`, on the boundary's steady clock); a side the boundary has
# no position for, or one too old, has not arrived and is UNHEARD. Before a
# person is asked into the cell the fixed program asks this in SIM with the
# plant's own track position: it waits while the answer is UNHEARD, and a
# physical carriage AWAY refuses the run there, before the prompt (S-08).
#
# SERVICE is the one place this name is written, as SetMode's is.

string SERVICE="/cite/twin/track_arrived"

string joint        # the track joint, as the plan names it
float64 position_m  # the target the program sent
float64 tolerance_m # the track's goal tolerance, as the plan states it
string[] sides      # the sides to judge, by the plan's side names (ADR-0072): exactly
                    # these, whatever the mode. Empty judges every side the current
                    # mode commands and every running physical side, as above. A side
                    # named that does not run is UNHEARD
---
# Why `arrived` is what it is. AWAY outranks UNHEARD: a carriage heard standing
# elsewhere does not clear by itself, a position not heard yet does.
uint8 ARRIVED=0      # every side asked about stands within tolerance of the target
uint8 AWAY=1         # a side heard (fresh, if physical) stands outside the tolerance
uint8 UNHEARD=2      # none is AWAY, but a side's position is not heard, or too old
uint8 NOT_A_TRACK=3  # `joint` is no track joint this zone's plan names

bool arrived        # reason == ARRIVED
uint8 reason        # one of the constants above
bool routed         # the current mode routes a track command through the twin
string detail       # which side is not there, and where it stands; or why none counts
